# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.js

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
# Any NEXT_DIST_DIR used to verify a build without clobbering a running
# dev server's .next — see the distDir note in next.config.js.
/.next-*/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# local env files
#
# Catch-all with one exception, rather than naming variants. `.env` and
# `.env*.local` were listed individually, which let `.env.backup-<timestamp>`
# through — the file crewchief-fix-key.command writes when it swaps a key. A
# `git add -A` then swept it into a commit and GitHub push protection caught
# the Supabase secret key and a GCP key in it. Nothing reached the remote.
.env*
!.env.example

# EAS non-interactive auth token (never commit)
#
# Its own line because no pattern already reaches it, and the reason is the
# name rather than the depth: `.env*` above does apply at every level
# (`apps/mobile/.env.backup` matches it), but `.easrc.local` does not begin
# `.env`, and `apps/mobile/.gitignore`s `.env*.local` does not match it either.
# The file is a bearer token for the Expo account that owns the build queue.
apps/mobile/.easrc.local

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# local working docs — never publish
DEBUG_EXPORT.md
DIAGNOSTIC_REPORT.md
IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md
TECH_DEBT_ASSESSMENT.md

# Cowork writes its outputs here, inside the repo. Untracked and unignored is
# the pairing that swept a Supabase key into a commit once already — the .env
# block above is that story — and this directory fills with prompts and reports
# nobody means to publish. Trailing slash because it is only ever a directory.
Claude outputs/

# scratch screenshots
public/image*.png

# agent worktrees — full checkouts of this repo, living inside it
#
# EAS flagged the project archive at 172 MB on build 29b4d76f (5 Aug). It was
# not node_modules or .next, both of which are already ignored: it was this
# directory at 433 MB, 428 MB of which is one spent worktree. Untracked and
# unignored means EAS packs it into the upload on **every** build, and there
# are only fifteen a month.
#
# `.claude/worktrees/` and not `.claude/`, because `.claude/launch.json` is
# tracked and is what the preview tooling reads.
#
# jest.config.js already excludes this path from both discovery and module
# resolution, for the same underlying reason: a full second copy of the repo
# sitting inside the repo is something every tool has to be told to ignore.
.claude/worktrees/

# Screenshot output from the design-critic loop (~/Developer/design-loop). PNGs
# at two viewports per iteration, and the same EAS-upload argument as
# `.claude/worktrees/` above: untracked and unignored means it ships in the
# build upload. `.env.agents` needs no line of its own — `.env*` already
# catches it, which is the point of the catch-all.
design-loop/
